Yay~ My third ascension, it's been like, a year now... I've had a few
close ascensions but like... they didn't go so well. I've been trying
for geno-wishless-polyless, but after awhile, I ended up getting
desperate, but... all of my previous adventurers who broke wishless
early died horrid scary deaths right around Medusa, involving large
summoning swarms, arch-liches before nice magic resistance showing up,
and other ickyness. Also, both of my totally serious attempts at
ascending genoless-wishless-polyless, that made it very far, died on
the planes, with the amulet. I love the messages though... in some
ways, dieing is more exciting than ascending.

I did one thing different this time around, which was... absolutely
positively no, playing while upset, horribly bored stiff, or like
playing while frustrated or frantic or when I'm feeling crappy. All of
that kept me from making lots of horribly stupid "oh that isn't so
dangerous, I'll just bop it" mistakes, and let me run away very very
fast and be better about things :)

After my latest silly ranger conduct total bomb (trying to get a
nuetral elf ranger, with vorpy, and the envoy of balance, yay! Just
sounds fun to me :p) I decided to go treasure hording rouge for some
silly reason. All my games are generally like...
genoless-wishless-polyless, this one just happened to work out.

Anyways, there were some firsts, I'd never really depended so heavily
on natural nurse dancing before, just nurses I found, I've never
really polymorphed into anything deliberately before, and like just
did it for icky polytraps and went oh foo, I lost my cloak, and also,
I've never killed so many dragons before just giving up on wishless to
get the dragon scale mail I want, but this was very fun, even if it
took forever :p

So many turns... anyways... Kat the Rouge started out horribly
normally, as a sleepy night boredom project, but something changed
after a bit, I decided not to play when horribly tired and late at
night, and that made all of the difference in the world. After working
down into the gnomish mines, and picking up daggers from nasty nasty
Gnomes, and taking a quick hoppie jump down a random hole in the
mines, I ended up in minetown. Nothing so special, just a single
oilskin sack in one of the shops, and the temple was not so nice to
me, oh well. I did find a nice Gauntlets of Power sometime around this
time, but I'm not sure when.

Worked down deep into the gnomish mines, it went s'kay, but my poor
pet dog Sirius followed me faithfully to the bottom of the mines. I
went all over, and... it was the "mimic at the bottom of the mines" I
had picked up an amulet of esp, so finding mimics was easy peasy,
but... I couldn't find the luckstone anywhere at all, and there was
one gnome tucked away in a little corner... Well, that gnome must have
grabbed the luckstone, that so must be it... so I slipped into the
little gap, walls too horribly hard to dig into after all, and blessed
up the stone. Since I was holding it, I got the rare chance to have
lodestones identified :)

I eventually found the luckstone, so that worked out okay, and pretty
much spent a good large amount of time that can be summed up as...
"busy busy, whack things bunches" and wander around trying to even out
my weight in the minetown temple, and also clear out all the meanie
shopkeepers aside from Izchak and the friendly general store owner. I
also bought out Izchaks entire store inventory, then sold it back
multiple times to give him a cozy profit, I was bored.

I moved on to sokuban, which was kinda uneventful, aside from a quick
hop around through the pits to go back to the beginning (all set up
right, I was just on the wrong side), but... so far I had really been
hoping for a nice bag of holding, the whole game I was kinda being
tied up for weight with an oilskin sack, but it made good practice.
Nothing special, and just an amulet of reflection *sigh* Better than
nothing I guess. One weird thing was I started throwing random things
at elves around this point, just so I could get elven daggers. *tosses
a ring at an elf* *makes elf grouchy* *steals daggers* When I hit 10,
all of them got a nice bonus later on.

I moved on, carefully working through levels, and having to make a few
drops off and make stashes to even out my weight, mostly giant giant
piles of scrolls, and a couple potion stashes. Potions seem to add up
so fast... at least I had most of them id'd by now, friendly unicorns,
and a dart or two helped lots. Weight is kinda a pain, and I'm a bag
of holding junkie.

When starting to approach the teenish levels I stumbled into a nasty
polytrap, and turned into a Vampire Lord... There went my nice "no
polyself" conduct, but encouraged me to try a few tricks later. It was
kinda nice for a little bit... but it led to a very close call when I
almost died, and had to teleport away, being a Vampire Lord... doesn't
give you that many hitpoints.

As I worked down I did a little bit of nurse dancing along the way,
picking up almost all of the health that I needed throughout the game,
aside from leveling. I mean... being in the mid 200s seemed like
totally plenty. It did get a little nasty here and there without
armor, so I used the opportunity to practice on hand-to-hand, just...
avoiding the 'trices.

On the way, I ran into a few friendly bone files, but... the best I
managed to get was just a few potions of holy water, and some food
rations, nothing really nasty or exciting (One ghost named No1 and
another... named something I can't remember, and forgot to write down
^^;) deep deep in the dungeon, around level 18 or so, I found the
bones file of a poor Valkyrie named Amy, who died... not so well so I
wont explain here. She left lots of pretty things in a couple bags of
holding, one was cursed, and the other wasn't and had some shiny
things. The Orb of Fate wasn't happy to be in the hands of a Rouge, so
it crawled to the corner of it's bag and stayed there. Nothing I could
do seemed to work when trying to pick the other bag up somehow, I had
totally foolishly forgotten you could cancel it. Part of me thinks
that there have to be more solutions to cursed items on the ground
than just zapping them with cancelation, I love my options :p (maybe
throwing holy water on the ground? or something weird like that?)

Amy also apparently died after looting out Fort Ludios, had a ton of
gold, and never gave it to the local friendly priest, so I made a very
large donation on her behalf.

I finally zapped it the bag with a wand of cancellation I picked up a
bit ago, did totally major renovations to make sure that I could get
my stash all working correctly, and moved on deeper into the dungeon.
I bumped into the quest, but wanted to avoid it until I had a ring of
protection from shapechangers, chamelions could be really nasty
otherwise... After traveling down and down... I bumped into Medusa's
isle... with a Titan sitting by the entrance... eek! I ran quickly
back up.. I wanted to live a little longer to get shinies. I killed a
ton of time trying to make sure I was okay and had the proper types of
rings (I had to dip a few of the nasty ones in fountains, saving on
holy water) After finally picking out the proper ring I headed for the
quest... only to back out after getting more seriously involved
because of all the polymorph traps... I needed magic resistance... I
had a tiny bit of luck in trying on my little pile of "cloaks with
weird funny names that are cursed right now" and happily went on my
way. The quest was easy peasy, all the way until I tried to fall into
the bottom level. I also got Grayswandir from her bags as well, which
made a very cozy gift... and... it's silver! *yays*

I landed on the far right... with no way to get out x.x; I could level
teleport... but nothing I typed in seemed to be really valid... so I
was totally stuck (I have no idea how to level teleport in branches
^^;) I wandered around a little... used some secret door detection
charges... and then... trapped the game in an infinite loop ...

It was a kinda serious bug, and I'll have to try reproducing it later,
but... I don't think it was a stuck keyboard, the turn counter just
kept going up, and nethack wouldn't respond to anything I said to it.
I was just getting to "hungry" so I acted fast and killed the game.
I've never ever gotten this far with a thief, I'm not about to lose it
to an out of game type error. Restarted, didn't get any weird bugs
this time, and it went mostly the same, but I was still totally
stuck...

I was getting a little desperate, so I started messing about with a
pleasant "polycontrol/polymorph" ring combination, but kept becoming a
"new man" or "new woman" over and over and over... no xorn *sigh*
After like... 10,000 turns I finally hit it, turned into a xorn, and
walked happily through the wall. I rewarded myself with a happy snack
of some gold pieces, and had an epic duel with the ebil Master
Assassin, winning with a blaze of flying daggers.

After happily taking my precious key and the bell I snuck off since
the Quest leader sounded like a horrid thug and a meanie. I wanted
shinies...

Working back down, I quickly dug through the floor in Medusa's lair,
then went up the stairs wearing a blindfold and the amulet of
reflection from sokubon, getting a sack, and the pair of levitation
boots from Perseus's statue *yay* Naturally... a ring I picked up one
level below Medusa was levitation, which I found out a little bit
after I was walking all over in flying boots.

I sacrificed until I turned blue, getting both Juiblex and Yengue, and
led both of them one level below minetown :3

I hunted around for Fort Ludios and finally stumbled into the portal.
I set myself up in the front room and cleared out the monsters then
went to the other door and used it as a choke point, wearing my amulet
of reflection ~just~ in case of nasties. I dabbled with a ring of
conflict for a few turns, decided it was horribly boring, and just
went to my usual wait and clear out the giant swarm as they come to
you approach, which worked very nicely. After getting rid of the small
army I went after Croesus, I floated over the moat, opened up the
door... and suddenly "Croesus zaps a jeweled wand" "The death ray hits
you, but it reflects off of your medallion!" After a nasty fight, and
trying to scramble to the wand amount a few angry trolls, and a
thieving hobgoblin who took it away from Croesus's corps, I tossed the
trolls in the moat and went happily on my way, carefully clearing out
the land mines by untrapping them in the treasure room, making a nice
hearty donation to a non aligned priest, then killing them off,
converting the altar to chaotic with the remaining corpse, and hauling
enough gold down to the local priest of Kos make me stressed while not
using my bag of holding (and burdened if I used it). I was very
appropriately chaotic this game :)

After Ludios, I moved on to clear out the castle. I had already gotten
the pass tune, all ready to play when... I realized I forgot my flute
several floors up in one of the stashes. Not so good... I guess I'll
have to fly around and so hope it doesn't turn out bad. I fly around
out back, no dragons gave scales *sigh* Except for one lone red
dragon... I tossed off my elven ring mail and switched it out... I
wanted to be able to cast spells finally. Oh and nothing special in
the castle armory, since a hungry Xorn went through and just left a
Helm of Opposite Alignment, eww. I flew over all of the trap doors,
burning a nice E-word in front of the door, and patiently worked
through lots of monsters. Disenchanters were kinda icky, I learned to
go after them with my pick-axe, it doesn't really need enchantment. I
collected the wand of wishing and enchanted up my daggers, dabbling a
little with some disenchanters to get them up to +7 (I didn't realize
that tossing them hurt with disenchanters, mojo never had that problem
at all....)

I sat on a throne boredly, got a wish... and decided... oh why not, I
don't feel like I need anything, maybe, make this an honest try for
wishless? I typed "nothing" and happily went on my way, deciding to
avoid thrones just for the heck of it.

What to do... I burned a scroll of genocide to get some silver dragons
by an altar, they turned out to heavy to sacrifice, and none of them
(even a couple of wands of raise undead, recharged several times) gave
scales...

Much more wandering... (I'm feeling this game is going on awhile, I
should level teleport more often, wandering between stashes is getting
kinda dull)

*much enchanting, marker scribbling, recharging later*

I enter Gehommen, wearing black dragon scales and some other cozy
armor, but this time with Gauntlets of Dexterity so that I don't have
so much trouble, oh and Grayswander and my silver saber both up to +7.
Gehommen pretty was lots of wandering and digging, aside from getting
another bag of holding (yay!) And later a t shirt, which made me very
happy, and quickly got all enchanted.

After awhile I level teleported up to minetown to see if I could get
something better, and clear out my other stashes. I got my spare
potions from minetown... I left a whole ton of unholy water there?
*yays* I go back to a cozy chaotic temple deep in the dungeon, call up
more silver dragons, and ~finally~ get scales from the last one I
kill. After that, not a single one of the silver dragons I killed gave
me scales either, or even the gray ones...

Much more wandering... a few demon princes... a ton of pet gremlins on
the Juiblex level (magic traps...) some polytraps, and a bit of
messyness, I found the stairs to Vlad's Tower. I didn't expect much...
Vlad's a total pushover... and the tower isn't that icky... It turned
out pretty wrong though... I walk in through the first door... and I'm
immidiately surrounded by a summoning storm from a Sunsword wielding
Archon... not so good... two yellow dragons and a green dragon are
biting me, along with a very grouchy looking elf lord hitting me over
the head. I hurriedly pull out some potions of full healing and start
frantically trying to burn the E-word in the floor with various
wands... three wands of lightning later I'm starting to get worried...
I have to start drinking potions... The Archon is still summoning up
hordes of monsters, and Vlad's Tower quickly becomes filled with
nasties... I notice a cockatrice a little bit away and quickly go
after it, using it to bop monsters over the head and (finally) get rid
of the Archon. I'm still having trouble with a few green dragons
biting at me and it's turning very horribly nasty, the corpse rots
away and I go back to digging through my bag in hopes of something
helpful, finally I think fast and burn the E-word with a working
wand... *sigh* Then fend off the dragons, and the last of the baddies
that didn't mind being bopped with a funny chicken. Still a few
dragons left, but I'm so healthy by now from getting some nurses help
that I'm doing wonderfully.

After the messyness I picked up the water walking boots, which looked
a little familiar... I had seen a pair in minetown, but tossed them
aside thinking they were like just normal boots, because of mixing
them up I'll be more careful iding boots next time. Moving on...

One of the worst little incidents on the way was a nasty little
encounter with a master mind flayer, I normally don't really have
trouble with them. You just have to make sure it can't get close at
all, and a few daggers usually makes it nice to handle them but... in
the twisty corners of Gehommen, I caught one just one square away with
a flurry of daggers and then "The master mindflayer's medallion begins
to glow" and it returned back to life! eek! It died quickly *lucky*
but... *shudder*

I worked all the way to the vibrating square, and left a little pile
of gold coins surrounding it, since I forgot my iron chain this time.
I think I might do that again later, since... it worked a lot better,
and wasn't so much weight to lug around xD

Some last minute prepping, and a little bit of skill exercise and
such, last minute stash ones, and making sure I was prepped for all of
the ascension run. I took a deep breath, looked at my little sprinkled
pile of gold around the vibrating square, then ran off to pay Rodney a
nice visit, picking up a pet purple worm on the way. The false
wizard's tower turned out to be a little strange, just a few lumps of
royal jelly, and mostly empty. I had a nagging suspicion that maybe it
was a bones level, but no sign of bones ever turned up, maybe buried
in the moat (*checks in the wizard mode save backup from just before
ascending* nope nope.)

I flew around the wizards towers, using a wand of digging to make a
passage, easily taking care of the vampires, and... picking up another
amulet of life saving underneath the vampire lord! Going on, I worked
through the zoo with a cockatrice corpse, bunches of whacking, and
some patience at the door. It worked out totally okay, and meeting up
with Rodney a little bit later wasn't that exciting. Just some flying
over the moat, and sorting through junk to toss into the moat that I
didn't need anymore. That papyrus spellbook weighs bunches...

Running down to the square, and performed the ceremony, and went down
with my pet into the inner sanctum. I left my little pet far behind
and stealthily cleaned out the graveyard, and headed towards the
altar. I used a cockatrice to get rid of the disenchanters by the
entrance, and cleaned out the rest with a little pet help and old
fashioned type poking, using a wand of secret door detection to find
the door to the temple and save a ton of time.

I swatted the high priest with a cockatrice. easier that way...
then... realized my wand of striking ran out of charges (no pick-axe,
it was left a few levels up) anyways... I ran all over looking chests,
turning over rocks, looking at all the little wand piles just looking
for something, and found a wand of striking in a chest in the
cemetery, yay! I went back, got the amulet from among the fresh pile
of rocks, and ran up whistling my pet to me, and reading off scrolls
of teleportation to get to stairs a little faster. On the way I made a
couple quick stops, one to sacrifice the Wizard of Yendor in the nice
chaotic temple (I got a succubus, and was frightened for a bit), and
also double bagged up my special shiny prizes with my extra bags of
holding. Finally... I stood on the stairs leading up, about to enter
the planes, I made some last minute preps, making sure that I got rid
of dead weight, and double checked everything... then... climbed the
stairs.

I faced Rodney on earth, read a cursed scroll of gold detection, and
zapped my way over to the portal, I had some minor battles with a few
Earth Elementals and... well, Earth was kinda dull, I walked through
the portal, and entered the Plane of Air. Again, I read a cursed
scroll to find the portal, put on a ring of levitation, and bumped
into an air elemental, while fighting my way out I thought... this
could get horribly icky. The next one I zapped with a wand of
polymorph and... it turned into a master mind flayer... eek! I tiptoed
caustiosly away and flew through the thunderous clouds only to get
very sad, because a black dragon blasted my poor purple worm *sigh*.

I was a little worried about entering the Plane of Fire, I'd lost one
character with this conduct there, so I used my handy crystal ball,
looked for traps, put on a towel, and just tried to dance around all
the icky monsters, traps, and whatever, and pray I didn't get caught
in a summoning storm. It worked out fine... and finally... the Plane
of Water. I had a few icky messes with some Krakens, and even lost the
grease on my cloak a couple times, which was really frightening. After
a moderate wait... I entered the Astral Plane.

I immediately took of my levitation ring, and floated to the ground,
then took a quick peek at who was guarding the altars. Death sat on
the left, Pestilence in the middle, and Famine guarded the far right.
Since I was kinda towards the left I went to challenge Death with my
new pet Angel. I tossed a few vollies of daggers and it worked out
okay, muddled through all the priests, some Liches, and adventures,
and met up with the altar... lawful *sigh* I headed back, only to have
a boulder thrown at my head as soon as I exited the door. I pushed
away the boulder, and used a swarm of insects to keep Death away.
Halfway through in the middle I kinda wondered a bit about whether or
not I should just go right... nah, the middle is closer. I zapped
Pestilence with a death ray, walked on, slogging through adventurers
and angels, and a couple pesky dragons, checked the altar and...
neutral *sigh* I guess... it's all three altars again this time? I
slogged back, zapping Pestilence again. Just in front of the door to
the right hand side I got trapped in a summoning storm from an
Arch-Lich. I burned the E-word quickly to keep back the dragons, and
got rid of the Arch-Lich. A grouchy giant tossed a boulder at me and I
used it to seal up the door while cleaning up the storm, them moved it
on and started tiptoeing along to the final altar. I quickly zapped
Famine, while avoiding a master mind flayer left over from the edge of
the storm, got all the way to the altar, Famine rose from the dead,
and just as it was nearing again....



